  "id": "gr-temiru",
  "connector": "〜てみる",
  "gloss": "try doing (and see)",
  "title": "〜てみる — try it and see",
  "pattern": "verb て form + みる",
  "explanation": "〜てみる is “do it and see”: trying something out. {食|た}べてみる — try eating it (and see what it’s like). It changes like みる: {食|た}べてみたい (I’d like to try it), {着|き}てみてもいいですか (may I try it on?), やってみて (give it a go).",
  "natural": "Perfect for food, clothes and new experiences: {一度|いちど}{温泉|おんせん}に{行|い}ってみたい — I’d like to try a hot spring once.",
  "stiff": "Trying hard to do something, and maybe failing, isn’t てみる but ようとする: {開|あ}けようとした — I tried to open it.",
  "examples": [
